dsv41 patch 0054 (20.10.2026): token embedding and DSpark Markov cache in the display reservation.
Base: vllm/v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py of image v5; uses vllm_exl3_moe/display_kv.py from patch 0053.
Why: rarely and contiguously read tensors could live in the 1,792 MiB display region and leave ordinary memory to the KV
pool. How: after target model and drafter are loaded, move_to_display copies the token embedding (631 MiB per rank) and
the Markov cache (505 MiB) into the display buffer with a kernel copy (bit-identical, checked) and points them there.
Measured (20.10.2026, GB10, 2000 MHz, image v6): KV 3.75 -> 4.75 GiB per rank (989,460 -> 1,253,309 tokens, without
0057), T=0 identical 8/8, but decode -1.7 % (geometric mean), 64K code -6.7 %, 3-4 streams -3...-4 %. Not adopted.
Switch: VLLM_DSV41_DISPLAY_TENSORS=1 (default off).

--- a/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py
@@ -410,6 +410,12 @@
